{
 "doc": "Shared golden for the share dialog's exact numbers: the browser's shareCountsFromTurns (frontend/app/conversation-share-disclosure.ts) and the server's counts endpoint (backend/app/domain/share_counts.py via GlobalAskStore.share_counts) must both produce `expected` for every scenario. Expansion (both sides): turn i has id t%04d and created_at 2026-01-01T00:00:00+00:00 plus s(i) seconds, written HH:MM:SS+00:00, where s(i)=i except inside a `ties` range [a, b] (a < i <= b: s(i)=s(a)); `images[i]` puts one image per listed asset id on its own anchor / citation; `legacy` turns are stored under `response` instead of `answer` (server only); `failed_after[i]` adds a failed job t%04d-f at turn i's instant (server only: never a turn). `through`: null = '', an index = that turn, 'missing' = 't-missing'. `watermark`: null = not shared, an index = that turn and its instant, {gone_at: i} = id 't-gone' (no such job) with turn i's instant.",
